1
00:00:10,599 --> 00:00:14,711
Orion was a young boy with a big dream: to learn how to fly.

2
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:21,411
Ever since he was very little, he had dreamed of soaring through the sky, and this autumn was no exception.

3
00:00:21,661 --> 00:00:24,259
One Saturday, Orion had a thought.

4
00:00:24,208 --> 00:00:27,267
If I'm going to fly, I need to make some wings!

5
00:00:27,517 --> 00:00:37,260
So he went to the garage and searched for materials. He found some empty cardboard boxes, and grabbed a pair of scissors and some tape from the workbench.

6
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:48,071
He spent a long time in the garage, cutting and shaping the cardboard into wing shapes. He used the tape to secure the wings to his arms, making sure they wouldn't fall off.

7
00:00:50,321 --> 00:00:59,766
Finally, his wings were ready. He walked out to the front yard, put on his wings, and started running around, flapping his arms as hard as he could.

8
00:00:59,816 --> 00:01:11,885
But no matter how fast he ran, or how high he jumped, he couldn't get off the ground. He flapped his arms as hard as he could, and ran as fast as he could, but he still could not fly.

9
00:01:12,035 --> 00:01:18,792
After a long time running around his front yard, Orion got tired, and sat down on the grass to rest.

10
00:01:19,042 --> 00:01:28,615
The golden sun was slowly starting to set, as it gently dipped below the horizon. The leaves on the trees rustled in the cool autumn breeze.

11
00:01:28,665 --> 00:01:36,318
The crisp air was filled with the scent of falling leaves, wood smoke, and the sweet aroma of ripe apples and pumpkins.

12
00:01:36,368 --> 00:01:38,111
Orion! Dinner time!

13
00:01:38,161 --> 00:01:45,579
He took off his wings and put them in the garage, then went inside to eat his favorite meal: spaghetti with meatballs.

14
00:01:47,829 --> 00:01:52,538
After dinner, Orion helped his mom and dad clean up and wash the dishes.

15
00:01:52,588 --> 00:02:01,627
Then he headed up to his bedroom to get ready for bed. His bedroom was his own personal retreat, a place where he could relax and be himself.

16
00:02:01,777 --> 00:02:14,144
His walls were covered in pictures of airplanes, birds, and superheroes, all of them flying through the air. Orion spent a few moments gazing at them, imagining what it would be like to fly.

17
00:02:14,394 --> 00:02:21,087
After changing into his pajamas and brushing his teeth, he climbed into bed and snuggled under the covers.

18
00:02:21,137 --> 00:02:28,683
He felt grateful for his warm, comfortable bed, and the roof over his head. He fell asleep with a smile on his face.

19
00:02:31,133 --> 00:02:34,434
The next morning, Orion woke up with a new idea.

20
00:02:34,384 --> 00:02:37,171
What if I put feathers on my cardboard wings?

21
00:02:37,221 --> 00:02:43,338
He was so excited that he jumped out of bed, got dressed quickly, and started running down the stairs.

22
00:02:43,188 --> 00:02:44,856
This just might work!

23
00:02:44,806 --> 00:02:46,443
No running down the stairs!

24
00:02:46,393 --> 00:02:49,758
This wasn't the first time she had reminded him of this rule.

25
00:02:49,708 --> 00:02:50,905
Yes, Mom.

26
00:02:50,955 --> 00:02:54,149
Eat your blueberry pancakes before you go out to play.

27
00:02:54,099 --> 00:02:55,132
Oh, man.

28
00:02:55,182 --> 00:03:03,005
He really just wanted to try out his new idea. But he eagerly finished his breakfast, and asked if he could go outside to play.

29
00:03:02,955 --> 00:03:04,250
Of course you can.

30
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:14,854
He leapt from the table with so much excitement that he almost knocked over his chair. He quietly put it back in place, and hurried out to the garage to get his cardboard wings.

31
00:03:17,104 --> 00:03:24,650
He gathered feathers from the chicken coop, trying his best not to disturb the chickens, who were busy clucking and pecking about.

32
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:35,147
As he searched for the perfect feathers, he couldn't help but laugh at the silly birds. One particularly mischievous chicken kept trying to sneak up and peck at his shoes.

33
00:03:35,297 --> 00:03:47,216
Orion gathered a good supply of feathers, and taped them to his homemade wings. He was so excited to test them out that he barely noticed the chicken that was now tugging at the hem of his shirt.

34
00:03:47,266 --> 00:03:48,479
This should work!

35
00:03:48,529 --> 00:03:52,022
He put on his feathery wings and ran out to the front yard.

36
00:03:54,272 --> 00:03:55,703
Here goes nothing!

37
00:03:55,652 --> 00:04:10,003
Orion took off running at top speed, flapping his arms as hard as he could. At first, he struggled to get off the ground, but he refused to give up. He kept running and flapping, panting and sweating as he ran.

38
00:04:10,153 --> 00:04:19,939
Eventually, he got tired and collapsed onto the grass, feeling a mix of frustration and determination. He couldn't help but wonder what he was doing wrong.

39
00:04:19,990 --> 00:04:23,098
Then, a sudden spark of inspiration hit him.

40
00:04:22,949 --> 00:04:25,384
Maybe I just need to jump higher!

41
00:04:25,435 --> 00:04:32,916
He ran back to the garage, rummaged through the clutter until he found a ladder and a rake, and hurried back to the front yard.

42
00:04:35,166 --> 00:04:48,557
It was late autumn, and the trees in Orion's yard were ablaze with color. Red, orange, pink, yellow, and brown. Most of the leaves had already fallen, creating a carpet of color across the lawn.

43
00:04:48,707 --> 00:04:54,697
He raked the leaves together into a large and fluffy heap, and placed the tall ladder right next to it.

44
00:04:54,747 --> 00:05:00,800
He climbed to the very top, started flapping his new wings, and then, with all his might, he jumped!

45
00:05:00,850 --> 00:05:09,420
Orion didn't fly at all. Instead, he fell right into the big pile of leaves, sending them flying up into the air around him.

46
00:05:09,470 --> 00:05:16,632
Even though he couldn't fly, it was still a lot of fun. So, laughing and tumbling, he tried it again, and again.

47
00:05:19,581 --> 00:05:25,463
A short time later, a garbage truck came rumbling down the street, and stopped in front of his house.

48
00:05:25,514 --> 00:05:39,225
The driver, a tall and burly man with a rough, stubbly face and large shoes, walked towards Orion. Despite his appearance, Orion could see kindness in the man's eyes as he knelt down to speak to him.

49
00:05:39,275 --> 00:05:41,364
Do you really want to learn to fly?

50
00:05:41,413 --> 00:05:42,828
More than anything.

51
00:05:42,978 --> 00:05:44,359
The man chuckled.

52
00:05:44,209 --> 00:05:47,903
If you really want to fly, then you can fly in your dreams.

53
00:05:47,954 --> 00:05:49,403
How do I do that?

54
00:05:49,454 --> 00:05:54,810
Practice, my boy. Practice. Just keep practicing, and never give up on your dream.

55
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:59,326
With a smile and a wave, the man returned to his truck and drove away.

56
00:05:59,377 --> 00:06:09,675
Orion lay in the leaves, gazing up at the sky, and made a promise to himself: to never give up on his dream of flying, and to practice every chance he got.

57
00:06:12,524 --> 00:06:22,204
That night, Orion climbed into his cozy bed in the corner of his room. The blankets were soft and thick, and always made him feel warm and secure.

58
00:06:22,254 --> 00:06:25,555
He wondered if he would be able to fly in his dreams.

59
00:06:25,605 --> 00:06:34,110
A short while later, his parents came into his room. His mother leaned down to kiss him on the forehead, her long hair tickling his face.

60
00:06:34,161 --> 00:06:37,054
Hey Dad, do you think I can fly in my dreams?

61
00:06:37,204 --> 00:06:38,906
I think you can.

62
00:06:39,055 --> 00:06:53,706
This made him very happy. He snuggled deeper into his blankets, already feeling the weightless sensation of flight in his mind. He let out a contented sigh, and before he knew it, he had drifted off into a deep and peaceful sleep.

63
00:06:57,455 --> 00:07:04,127
He could hear the howling wind outside, and the tapping of a branch on his window. Tap. Tap. Tap.

64
00:07:04,476 --> 00:07:14,433
The noise almost woke him up, but he did not want to wake up, because he was having a really good dream. Then he remembered: he should try to fly in his dreams!

65
00:07:14,483 --> 00:07:22,200
So in his dream, he started flapping his arms and tried to run super fast. But it felt like he was running through honey.

66
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:29,113
The thick, sticky honey slowed every step. His feet felt stuck to the ground, his legs heavy and sluggish.

67
00:07:29,264 --> 00:07:41,694
Frustrated, he dreamed instead about his friends, and the swimming pool they used to visit every summer. The sound of laughter and splashing as they played and swam. That was a very nice dream.

68
00:07:44,144 --> 00:07:52,096
The next morning, Orion's mind was still racing from the night's dream. It had been so hard to run that he could not even jump!

69
00:07:52,146 --> 00:07:59,584
He could vividly recall every detail, from the cool night air, to the way his heart seemed to pulse with the power of flight.

70
00:07:59,634 --> 00:08:03,149
He thought about this for a while, until he got a new idea.

71
00:08:03,098 --> 00:08:07,333
Maybe if I wear my Superman cape, it will help me fly in my sleep!

72
00:08:07,483 --> 00:08:12,661
So that night, before he went to bed, he put on his cape. And then, he fell asleep.

73
00:08:15,711 --> 00:08:23,492
A few hours later, Orion found himself back in the dream world, determined to fly. He knew that this was his chance.

74
00:08:23,542 --> 00:08:35,099
This time, he had on his cape. It was made of a shiny red fabric that flowed behind him as he moved. It always made him feel like a superhero, ready to take on any challenge.

75
00:08:35,149 --> 00:08:42,331
He really believed he could do it this time. So, in his dream, he jumped into the air as hard as he could!

76
00:08:42,481 --> 00:08:46,273
Then, a very amazing thing happened. He started to fly!

77
00:08:46,523 --> 00:08:53,577
He was floating in the air, like a bubble. But when he tried to control his flying, he once again had a hard time.

78
00:08:55,827 --> 00:09:02,158
Orion spread his arms out in front of him, just like Superman, and for a moment, it seemed to work.

79
00:09:02,107 --> 00:09:04,588
Maybe Superman flies with his hands?

80
00:09:04,639 --> 00:09:13,465
But flying with his hands was a lot harder than he expected. His movements felt wobbly and uncertain, like balancing on a tightrope.

81
00:09:13,514 --> 00:09:15,994
Maybe Superman flies with his thumbs?

82
00:09:16,043 --> 00:09:24,634
That was even more difficult! Every time he moved his thumbs, even just a little bit, his body would zip sharply in that direction.

83
00:09:24,684 --> 00:09:26,644
Well, that's not going to work!

84
00:09:26,693 --> 00:09:34,004
Flying in his dreams was a lot harder than he had imagined. But even so, he wasn't ready to give up just yet.

85
00:09:36,154 --> 00:09:40,562
Maybe Superman can fly so well because of the letter S on his chest!

86
00:09:40,613 --> 00:09:49,354
So Orion stuck out his chest and began to fly. And amazingly, something was very different this time. He could control his flying!

87
00:09:49,403 --> 00:10:01,686
The further he pushed out his chest, the faster he would fly. When he pulled his chest back, he could easily slow down. And when he moved his chest to the left and the right, he would fly that way too!

88
00:10:01,936 --> 00:10:04,404
But then, Orion thought to himself:

89
00:10:04,254 --> 00:10:07,484
I don't have an S on my chest. So how can I do it?

90
00:10:07,834 --> 00:10:10,567
Maybe... it's my heart that makes me fly!

91
00:10:14,317 --> 00:10:26,322
Orion's heart was so full of love for flying, that it made his heart very powerful. So he opened his heart all the way, as much as he could, and let all his love for flying guide him.

92
00:10:26,472 --> 00:10:35,470
He flew higher and higher, laughing with joy as the wind rushed past him. It was the most amazing feeling he had ever experienced.

93
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:39,518
He flew all around the neighborhood. Over houses, and trees.

94
00:10:39,567 --> 00:10:40,970
Through the clouds.

95
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:42,521
And over the moon!

96
00:10:42,871 --> 00:10:50,716
He flew higher and higher, until he was soaring through the starry sky. It was the most incredible adventure of his life.

97
00:10:50,866 --> 00:10:54,466
Then he began to fly faster, and faster, and faster!

98
00:10:58,415 --> 00:11:03,636
Orion flew so incredibly fast in his dreams that night, that he lost his shoes!

99
00:11:03,787 --> 00:11:08,922
His shoes came right off his feet, because his shoelaces were not tied on tight enough.

100
00:11:09,271 --> 00:11:13,958
And that is why, if you ever see a pair of shoes hanging from a telephone wire...

101
00:11:14,109 --> 00:11:17,302
they were lost by kids who were flying in their dreams.

102
00:11:21,952 --> 00:11:26,063
From that day on, Orion was known as the boy who could fly.

103
00:11:26,213 --> 00:11:31,092
He flew in his dreams all the time, exploring the world, and having adventures.

104
00:11:31,243 --> 00:11:36,229
And every time he flew, he remembered the long journey it had taken him to get there.

105
00:11:36,379 --> 00:11:41,577
But it was all worth it, because he had finally achieved his dream of learning how to fly.

106
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:43,474
The end.
